00:32:18.690 --> 00:32:22.150
it, like, commitment is one of those things, you want everybody else to commit to you, but we don't

00:32:22.150 --> 00:32:27.250
want to commit to anything. Like, that's just kind of how it works. But in the Bible, like, the

00:32:27.250 --> 00:32:32.590
descriptions of the church we see, like, the most common descriptions of the church are a spiritual

00:32:32.590 --> 00:32:39.750
family or a body with many parts. And if you think about that, like, a family, do you, is it like one

00:32:39.750 --> 00:32:43.270
day you're part of a family and the next day you're not part of the family and the next day you're back

00:32:43.270 --> 00:32:48.050
in again. No, it's like if you're part of a family, you're in the family. You're committed to those

00:32:48.050 --> 00:32:52.710
relationships. How about with your body? Do you like take off your arm one day and like reattach

00:32:52.710 --> 00:32:57.810
it the next? Like no, you're a part of the body. You have a meaningful role. You're important

00:32:57.810 --> 00:33:02.410
as part of that body. And this is something we want to encourage. I mean, many of you here,

00:33:02.450 --> 00:33:05.830
you're checking out different churches and ministries. That's great. What I would share

00:33:05.830 --> 00:33:09.350
with you is you don't need to commit to this church. We would love it if you did. If you're

00:33:09.350 --> 00:33:13.250
not going to commit to this church. Commit to another church, because that's going to help you

00:33:13.250 --> 00:33:17.070
grow spiritually. That's going to be valuable for your growth, and that's going to build up others

00:33:17.070 --> 00:33:21.530
around you as well. And so we want people to believe in the gospel and commit to the church, to be part

00:33:21.530 --> 00:33:27.850
of this worshiping, growing, praying, serving community. And then as we do that, we also want

00:33:27.850 --> 00:33:32.710
everyone to become a disciple who seeks Jesus, serves, and is sent to make disciples. And we'll

00:33:32.710 --> 00:33:37.710
look at another picture of this next week in Acts chapter 13. But notice Jesus said, teach them to

00:33:37.710 --> 00:33:42.570
observe all that I have commanded you? Well, it's hard to sum up everything Jesus commanded us to do.

00:33:42.770 --> 00:33:47.930
That's a lot. But think about some basic things, like seeking Jesus, like having an abiding

00:33:47.930 --> 00:33:53.190
relationship with Christ, like we see in John 15, that we abide in him and we bear much fruit. Or

00:33:53.190 --> 00:33:58.130
like serving. Matthew writes in Matthew 23, Jesus said, the greatest among you will be your servant.

00:33:58.610 --> 00:34:03.470
That's what Jesus modeled and demonstrated for us. He wants us to be those who serve. And then today

00:34:03.470 --> 00:34:08.230
we're talking about being sent to make disciples, and that's in so many ways. We can make disciples

00:34:08.230 --> 00:34:13.210
around our campus and city as we reach out to different people, or even through things like

00:34:13.210 --> 00:34:18.490
short-term missions trips that we do as a church, or through one-year internships with AMI that

00:34:18.490 --> 00:34:22.850
we're part of, or through intentionally discipling our children as they grow up within our

00:34:22.850 --> 00:34:28.710
households, or maybe starting a Bible study at work, investing in the next generation, or leading

00:34:28.710 --> 00:34:33.390
a life group or ministry team. There are all these different ways that we can actually live

00:34:33.390 --> 00:34:37.950
out our faith in that being sent to make disciples. But imagine for a moment, these are kind of big

00:34:37.950 --> 00:34:42.770
ideas, but just imagine what this could look like for you. I know for many of us, many people

00:34:42.770 --> 00:34:47.030
share with me, starting a new season, there's a lot of anxiety that comes with that. Maybe some

00:34:47.030 --> 00:34:51.470
of us here, we're actually feeling really anxious about starting college, starting grad school,

00:34:51.950 --> 00:34:56.630
starting high school, starting, you know, whatever else it may be, starting a new job, new season of

00:34:56.630 --> 00:35:03.690
family, new kids on the way, feel this anxiousness about this, what would it be like to bring that

00:35:03.690 --> 00:35:09.590
anxiety to a community, a biblical community of grace and truth, to there be supported and

00:35:09.590 --> 00:35:15.770
encouraged by the love of God, to be invited into the grace and mercy of Jesus, to be really lifted

00:35:15.770 --> 00:35:20.990
up from that, and then like, wow, I can come on a Sunday, and even in the midst of my struggles

00:35:20.990 --> 00:35:25.790
and my doubts, I can still be part of a worshiping community, or I fix my eyes on Jesus, I realize

00:35:25.790 --> 00:35:30.410
he's bigger than those things that I feel so much anxiety about. And I hear God's word and I learn

00:35:30.410 --> 00:35:37.150
to trust and believe and follow Jesus. And God is setting me free from that anxiety as I seek him

00:35:37.150 --> 00:35:42.030
and worship him. And then while I go to class and I see somebody else struggling with anxiety, I go

00:35:42.030 --> 00:35:46.590
to work, I see somebody else struggling, and man, now I have something to share with them. I can

00:35:46.590 --> 00:35:51.670
invite them into the same grace and mercy that I have experienced and live that out together. This

00:35:51.670 --> 00:35:57.450
what that can look like on a regular basis. And I think for us as a church, this is what we need to

00:35:57.450 --> 00:36:02.650
kind of wrestle with, is what kind of church community will we be? Will we be a community of

00:36:02.650 --> 00:36:08.170
faith that really lives this out together, or will we settle for something else? I realize that

00:36:08.170 --> 00:36:13.530
churches around the world, around the country, see themselves in different ways. Some of you may have

00:36:13.530 --> 00:36:17.610
grown up in lots of different kinds of churches, which is awesome. There are some churches that

00:36:17.610 --> 00:36:23.570
see themselves as maybe maintaining a denominational or theological tradition. That's great. Maybe other

00:36:23.570 --> 00:36:28.710
churches see themselves rooted as like a more of a cultural or ethnic church that is about that

00:36:28.710 --> 00:36:34.830
tradition, that background. That's great. Maybe for others, it's different things. It's, you know,

00:36:34.830 --> 00:36:39.230
like a club or a friend group to be part of, people to hang out with and have a good time with,

00:36:39.250 --> 00:36:43.910
or maybe even as a spiritual business, delivering Christian goods and services, and you pay your

00:36:43.910 --> 00:36:49.370
do somehow. It could be all kinds of stuff. I thank God that he works in all different kinds of

00:36:49.370 --> 00:36:54.410
churches. I praise God for that. For us as a church, what are we going to be? I really pray that we

00:36:54.410 --> 00:37:00.910
will see ourselves and understand ourselves as a church that's built on a mission, a mission that

00:37:00.910 --> 00:37:05.610
we believe Jesus has called us to. And that, again, that mission is transforming lost people

00:37:05.610 --> 00:37:09.770
into Christ's disciples who will then transform the world. And what we really believe, and the

00:37:09.770 --> 00:37:14.530
reason our church is here on the U of M campus and in Ann Arbor, Michigan, is we really believe that

00:37:14.530 --> 00:37:20.370
if lives are transformed here, that the world will literally be transformed around us. I love

00:37:20.370 --> 00:37:24.710
it that the nations of the world gather here in Ann Arbor, over a hundred nations on the U of M

00:37:24.710 --> 00:37:29.730
campus. I love it that the next generation comes here for training and to prepare for the rest of

00:37:29.730 --> 00:37:33.950
their lives. Literally, if we live out our faith and if we live out this mission here, the people

00:37:33.950 --> 00:37:37.950
that we reach, the people who grow as disciples in our church, the people we live out our faith

00:37:37.950 --> 00:37:42.450
together with here will go around the country and to the ends of the earth and will literally

00:37:42.450 --> 00:37:46.590
change the world because of what they've experienced here within our church community.

00:37:47.390 --> 00:37:53.130
And so what could this look like as we live out our mission together this year? God's been really

00:37:53.130 --> 00:37:58.090
faithful to our church over the last 30 years. And as we look ahead, I know for some of us, maybe

00:37:58.090 --> 00:38:03.030
there's even a struggle or a doubt that comes with this. Maybe for some of us like, man, I want

00:38:03.030 --> 00:38:09.030
to live for something bigger than myself. I want to be part of a global calling. I want to be part

00:38:09.030 --> 00:38:17.270
of what God's doing in the world, but I doubt. I feel inadequate. I struggle. I'm not sure if I'm

00:38:17.270 --> 00:38:23.330
good enough for this. I don't know what impact I could have on the lives of others. I'm not sure

00:38:23.330 --> 00:38:28.750
how to just manage myself right now. But you know, here's where I love it, that whenever God gives us

00:38:28.750 --> 00:38:30.530
a calling, he also gives us a promise.

00:38:31.350 --> 00:38:32.810
And when Jesus gave this calling,

00:38:33.250 --> 00:38:34.750
go and make disciples of all nations,

00:38:35.690 --> 00:38:36.830
he also said,

00:38:36.990 --> 00:38:37.830
I'm going to be with you.

00:38:38.550 --> 00:38:40.950
I'm going to be with you. And this is the confidence

00:38:40.950 --> 00:38:42.830
that we can have today as we look ahead

00:38:42.830 --> 00:38:44.830
into this coming year. Jesus is going

00:38:44.830 --> 00:38:46.930
to be with us in all the struggles

00:38:46.930 --> 00:38:48.950
we face, in all the doubts that we need

00:38:48.950 --> 00:38:50.910
to try to figure out, in all

00:38:50.910 --> 00:38:52.790
the temptations that we need to say

00:38:52.790 --> 00:38:55.110
no to, in all the opportunities

00:38:55.110 --> 00:38:56.390
that we need to say yes to.

00:38:56.710 --> 00:38:58.850
Jesus is going to be with us through all of that.

00:38:59.490 --> 00:39:00.550
And so as we wrap up this time,

00:39:00.590 --> 00:39:02.270
I just want to give you just three quick things

00:39:02.270 --> 00:39:04.690
to think about reflecting and responding to this morning.

00:39:05.150 --> 00:39:06.770
The first of those is I just want to encourage you

00:39:06.770 --> 00:39:08.750
to hear Jesus' calling personally.

00:39:09.390 --> 00:39:10.810
Hear Jesus' calling personally.

00:39:11.330 --> 00:39:13.130
I believe that this calling, the Great Commission,

00:39:13.250 --> 00:39:14.610
I believe it's given to the church

00:39:14.610 --> 00:39:16.410
and it's given to every individual Christian.

00:39:17.150 --> 00:39:18.410
Can you hear this as a calling

00:39:18.410 --> 00:39:21.270
not just to this church, this organization today,

00:39:21.750 --> 00:39:23.970
but as a calling that you yourself would hear

00:39:23.970 --> 00:39:25.310
and be part of,

00:39:25.310 --> 00:39:27.490
that Jesus is speaking to you today,

00:39:28.270 --> 00:39:29.190
calling you by name,

00:39:29.250 --> 00:39:31.010
saying, I want you to be part of this.

00:39:31.410 --> 00:39:32.810
Can you hear that personally today?

00:39:32.870 --> 00:39:35.290
I know this is a calling of Jesus on your life.

00:39:35.790 --> 00:39:37.110
The second thing I would encourage you with

00:39:37.110 --> 00:39:39.630
is to prayerfully consider your next steps in this.

00:39:40.150 --> 00:39:41.290
What does that look like for you?

00:39:41.850 --> 00:39:42.550
And for some of you,

00:39:42.610 --> 00:39:44.010
maybe you're just here for the first time,

00:39:44.070 --> 00:39:44.890
you're checking things out,

00:39:44.930 --> 00:39:46.510
and maybe a great first step

00:39:46.510 --> 00:39:48.430
would actually be to sign up for a life group

00:39:48.430 --> 00:39:49.430
like we've been talking about.

00:39:50.050 --> 00:39:50.770
For some of you,

00:39:50.990 --> 00:39:52.510
maybe it's actually doing other things

00:39:52.510 --> 00:39:54.490
like getting involved in serving in our church

00:39:54.490 --> 00:39:56.810
because, wow, yeah, I want to be somebody who serves

00:39:56.810 --> 00:39:58.010
like Jesus told me to.

00:39:58.070 --> 00:40:00.690
I want to grow in that in some way this year.

00:40:01.250 --> 00:40:02.910
Maybe it's growing your devotional life,

00:40:02.990 --> 00:40:06.170
learning to seek Jesus day by day in his word and in prayer.

00:40:06.490 --> 00:40:08.250
Maybe it's learning to mentor somebody.

00:40:08.530 --> 00:40:10.810
I had a great experience in my life group last year.

00:40:11.070 --> 00:40:13.390
I want to do that for somebody else this year.

00:40:13.390 --> 00:40:15.530
I want to mentor somebody and take them under my wing.

00:40:15.770 --> 00:40:17.410
I want to disciple the next generation.

00:40:18.130 --> 00:40:20.650
Maybe it's actually inviting somebody to come and join you

00:40:20.650 --> 00:40:22.850
next Sunday or at your first life group meeting

00:40:22.850 --> 00:40:23.590
that you'll go to.

00:40:24.250 --> 00:40:26.550
Maybe it's praying for someone in the classroom

00:40:26.550 --> 00:40:27.410
or in the workplace

00:40:27.410 --> 00:40:30.010
because you know they're struggling with some things.

00:40:30.730 --> 00:40:31.750
Prayerfully consider that.

00:40:31.830 --> 00:40:33.410
I can't give you all the ideas

00:40:33.410 --> 00:40:35.350
that God might actually speak to you about,

00:40:35.570 --> 00:40:36.470
but pray about that and say,

00:40:36.550 --> 00:40:38.390
God, how do you want me to take my next steps?

00:40:38.810 --> 00:40:41.010
And then third, don't settle for a temporary purpose.

00:40:42.110 --> 00:40:43.710
We'll talk about this quite a bit this year.

00:40:44.110 --> 00:40:45.810
Don't settle for a temporary purpose.

00:40:46.370 --> 00:40:48.090
I would encourage all of us to realize today

00:40:48.090 --> 00:40:51.190
we are where we are for a reason bigger

00:40:51.190 --> 00:40:53.930
than we usually remember on a day-to-day basis.

00:40:54.250 --> 00:40:56.510
For some of us, that's raising our kids.

00:40:57.290 --> 00:40:59.610
For some of us, that's going to school,

00:40:59.750 --> 00:41:00.670
middle school, high school.

00:41:01.110 --> 00:41:03.510
For some of us, that's going to our workplace day by day

00:41:03.510 --> 00:41:05.210
or whatever else it is that you're called to.

00:41:05.730 --> 00:41:06.850
For some of you here, especially,

00:41:07.010 --> 00:41:09.550
and many of you today, you're here for the first time

00:41:09.550 --> 00:41:10.890
going to the University of Michigan

00:41:10.890 --> 00:41:12.350
as a college or a grad student.

00:41:12.990 --> 00:41:15.070
You're here at one of the best universities in the world.

00:41:15.190 --> 00:41:16.730
Time Magazine says number five in the world.

00:41:16.810 --> 00:41:17.390
Can you believe that?

00:41:17.670 --> 00:41:18.370
I think it's number one.

00:41:18.370 --> 00:41:22.590
you're here can you know that you're here for a purpose bigger than yourself

00:41:22.590 --> 00:41:28.350
not just to collect a degree a piece of paper get the right go the right major figure out your

00:41:28.350 --> 00:41:33.030
next steps god has a purpose for you here and your education is part of it but as he has a purpose

00:41:33.030 --> 00:41:38.510
for you here to be part of his mission and his calling in the world in the church that's a joyful

